// spec: DCL-006
//
// ⚠️ A defect is a statement about the INTERPRETER and is never compiled.
//
// ⚠️ THE FUNCTION HALF IS FIXED.  A call above a function works; see
// conformance/0122.
//
// A CLASS is still not hoisted, so constructing one written below fails.  The
// reason it was not done with the functions: a class declaration EVALUATES its
// superclass, so hoisting the declaration hoists the evaluation -- which broke
// 'class B (A); ... class A;' and made CLS-014's ''X'' is not a class.'
// unreachable for any name declared in the same file.  It needs a two-phase
// declaration: bind the name at hoist time, resolve the superclass where the
// declaration stands.

var D := Dog ();

class Dog;
begin
    constructor Init (); begin end
end

WriteLn (D is Dog);
